# The parser corpus: every example of docs/language.md, one per line.
#
#   input ⇒ parse-form                  the statements' parse forms (§1), joined by " | ";
#                                       a quiet statement ends with ";"
#   input ⇒ error L:C: message          the message of §16 and its position
#   input ⇒ tree: <debug form>          the raw tree's toString, where the parse form cannot
#                                       tell a vector from a list
#   [after f(t) := t^2] input ⇒ …       parsed after that definition
#
# Every input is parsed as a script in the empty environment. "\n", "\t" and "\uXXXX" in an
# input are escapes.
# A "# §N" line names the section the following entries come from.

# §2 Source text
xy ⇒ xy
x y ⇒ x*y
2e-3 ⇒ 0.002
2e - 3 ⇒ 2*e - 3
5!=3 ⇒ 5 != 3
5! = 3 ⇒ factorial(5) = 3
x(x+1) ⇒ x*(x + 1)
x (x+1) ⇒ x*(x + 1)
sin(x) ⇒ sin(x)
sin (x) ⇒ sin(x)
x # a comment ⇒ x
x\u00A0y\tz ⇒ x*y*z
\uFEFFx + 1 ⇒ x + 1
a := 5;\nb := a + 1\nb^2 ⇒ a := 5; | b := a + 1 | b^2
a; b ⇒ a; | b
;;\n\n ⇒
(a; b) ⇒ error 1:3: unexpected `;`
x +\n1 ⇒ error 1:4: expected an operand
(x +\n1) ⇒ x + 1
x + 1 + ⇒ error 1:8: expected an operand
x y ⇒ x*y

